{"id":"mahabharata-6-095","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":95,"title":"पञ्चनवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 95 · Ninth day: the armies set out","summary":{"en":"At dawn Duryodhana orders the army out and tells his brothers to guard Bhishma above all. The Kauravas under Bhishma and the Pandavas under Bhima march out, and the din rises.","kn":"ಉದಯದಲ್ಲಿ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ಹೊರಡಿಸಿ ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ಎಲ್ಲಕ್ಕಿಂತ ಮುಖ್ಯವಾಗಿ ಕಾಯುವಂತೆ ತಮ್ಮಂದಿರಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ನೇತೃತ್ವದಲ್ಲಿ ಕೌರವರು, ಭೀಮನ ನೇತೃತ್ವದಲ್ಲಿ ಪಾಂಡವರು ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"भोर में दुर्योधन सेना को निकलने का आदेश देता है और भाइयों से कहता है कि सबसे बढ़कर भीष्म की रक्षा करें। भीष्म के नेतृत्व में कौरव और भीम के नेतृत्व में पाण्डव कूच करते हैं।","te":"ఉదయం దుర్యోధనుడు సేనను బయలుదేరమని ఆజ్ఞాపించి, ముఖ్యంగా భీష్ముని కాపాడమని సోదరులకు చెబుతాడు. భీష్ముని నాయకత్వంలో కౌరవులు, భీముని నాయకత్వంలో పాండవులు బయలుదేరతారు.","ta":"விடியலில் துரியோதனன் படையை அனுப்பி, எல்லாவற்றிலும் முக்கியமாகப் பீஷ்மரைக் காக்கும்படி சகோதரர்களுக்குக் கூறுகிறான். பீஷ்மர் தலைமையில் கௌரவரும் பீமன் தலைமையில் பாண்டவரும் புறப்படுகின்றனர்.","ml":"പ്രഭാതത്തിൽ സേനയെ പുറത്തിറക്കാൻ ദുര്യോധനൻ കൽപ്പിക്കുന്നു; ഭീഷ്മരെ എല്ലാറ്റിനുമുപരി സംരക്ഷിക്കാൻ സഹോദരന്മാരോട് പറയുന്നു. ഭീഷ്മരുടെ കീഴിൽ കൗരവരും ഭീമന്റെ കീഴിൽ പാണ്ഡവരും പുറപ്പെടുന്നു; ആരവം ഉയരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.95; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रभातायां तु शर्वर्यां प्रातरुत्थाय वै नृपः ।\nराज्ञः समाज्ञापयत सेनां योजयतेति ह ।\nअद्य भीष्मो रणे क्रुद्धो निहनिष्यति सोमकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When night had turned to dawn, the king rose in the morning and ordered the army made ready, saying, \"Today Bhishma, in his anger, will slay the Somakas in battle.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"दुर्योधनस्य तच्छ्रुत्वा रात्रौ विलपितं बहु ।\nमन्यमानः स तं राजन्प्रत्यादेशमिवात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard Duryodhana's long lament that night, O king, Bhishma took it as a rebuke to himself."}},{"n":3,"text":"निर्वेदं परमं गत्वा विनिन्द्य परवाच्यताम् ।\nदीर्घं दध्यौ शांतनवो योद्धुकामोऽर्जुनं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deeply dejected and blaming how people speak of others, Shantanu's son brooded long, wishing to fight Arjuna in the battle."}},{"n":4,"text":"इङ्गितेन तु तज्ज्ञात्वा गाङ्गेयेन विचिन्तितम् ।\nदुर्योधनो महाराज दुःशासनमचोदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reading the thoughts of the son of Ganga from his expression, great king, Duryodhana urged Duhshasana on."}},{"n":5,"text":"दुःशासन रथास्तूर्णं युज्यन्तां भीष्मरक्षिणः ।\nद्वात्रिंशत्त्वमनीकानि सर्वाण्येवाभिचोदय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Duhshasana, have the chariots that guard Bhishma yoked quickly, and rouse all thirty-two divisions of the army."}},{"n":6,"text":"इदं हि समनुप्राप्तं वर्षपूगाभिचिन्तितम् ।\nपाण्डवानां ससैन्यानां वधो राज्यस्य चागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This moment we have thought about for many years has come: the killing of the Pandavas with their army, and the winning of the kingdom."}},{"n":7,"text":"तत्र कार्यमहं मन्ये भीष्मस्यैवाभिरक्षणम् ।\nस नो गुप्तः सुखाय स्याद्धन्यात्पार्थांश्च संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think our task here is to protect Bhishma alone. Guarded, he will bring us happiness and will kill the Parthas in the fight."}},{"n":8,"text":"अब्रवीच्च विशुद्धात्मा नाहं हन्यां शिखण्डिनम् ।\nस्त्रीपूर्वको ह्यसौ जातस्तस्माद्वर्ज्यो रणे मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"That pure-hearted man has said, 'I will not kill Shikhandin; he was born first as a woman, so I must avoid him in the fight.'"}},{"n":9,"text":"लोकस्तद्वेद यदहं पितुः प्रियचिकीर्षया ।\nराज्यं स्फीतं महाबाहो स्त्रियश्च त्यक्तवान्पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The world knows, mighty-armed one, that to please my father I once gave up a flourishing kingdom and the company of women."}},{"n":10,"text":"नैव चाहं स्त्रियं जातु न स्त्रीपूर्वं कथंचन ।\nहन्यां युधि नरश्रेष्ठ सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will never, best of men, kill a woman in battle, nor anyone who was once a woman. I tell you this truly."}},{"n":11,"text":"अयं स्त्रीपूर्वको राजञ्शिखण्डी यदि ते श्रुतः ।\nउद्योगे कथितं यत्तत्तथा जाता शिखण्डिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you have heard, O king, of Shikhandin as one first a woman, as was told at the time of the preparations, that is how Shikhandini came to be:"}},{"n":12,"text":"कन्या भूत्वा पुमाञ्जातः स च योत्स्यति भारत ।\nतस्याहं प्रमुखे बाणान्न मुञ्चेयं कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"born a girl, then turned into a man, and he will fight, Bharata. I will in no way loose arrows in front of him."}},{"n":13,"text":"युद्धे तु क्षत्रियांस्तात पाण्डवानां जयैषिणः ।\nसर्वानन्यान्हनिष्यामि संप्राप्तान्बाणगोचरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But in battle, dear friend, I will kill all other Kshatriyas who wish for the Pandavas' victory and come within range of my arrows.'"}},{"n":14,"text":"एवं मां भरतश्रेष्ठो गाङ्गेयः प्राह शास्त्रवित् ।\nतत्र सर्वात्मना मन्ये भीष्मस्यैवाभिपालनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus the son of Ganga, best of the Bharatas, learned in the scriptures, spoke to me. Therefore I think we should guard Bhishma with our whole selves."}},{"n":15,"text":"अरक्ष्यमाणं हि वृको हन्यात्सिंहं महावने ।\nमा वृकेणेव शार्दूलं घातयेम शिखण्डिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"For even a wolf can kill an unguarded lion in a great forest. Let us not have a tiger killed by a wolf like Shikhandin."}},{"n":16,"text":"मातुलः शकुनिः शल्यः कृपो द्रोणो विविंशतिः ।\nयत्ता रक्षन्तु गाङ्गेयं तस्मिन्गुप्ते ध्रुवो जयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let my uncle Shakuni, Shalya, Kripa, Drona, and Vivimshati take care to guard the son of Ganga. When he is protected, victory is sure.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा तु राजानो दुर्योधनवचस्तदा ।\nसर्वतो रथवंशेन गाङ्गेयं पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Duryodhana's words, the kings surrounded the son of Ganga on every side with a line of chariots."}},{"n":18,"text":"पुत्राश्च तव गाङ्गेयं परिवार्य ययुर्मुदा ।\nकम्पयन्तो भुवं द्यां च क्षोभयन्तश्च पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons also went joyfully around the son of Ganga, making the earth and sky tremble and unsettling the Pandavas."}},{"n":19,"text":"तै रथैश्च सुसंयुक्तैर्दन्तिभिश्च महारथाः ।\nपरिवार्य रणे भीष्मं दंशिताः समवस्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With their well-harnessed chariots and elephants, the armoured great warriors stood surrounding Bhishma in the battle."}},{"n":20,"text":"यथा देवासुरे युद्धे त्रिदशा वज्रधारिणम् ।\nसर्वे ते स्म व्यतिष्ठन्त रक्षन्तस्तं महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As in the war of the gods and demons the gods stood around the wielder of the thunderbolt, so they all stood protecting that great chariot-fighter."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा पुनर्भ्रातरमब्रवीत् ।\nसव्यं चक्रं युधामन्युरुत्तमौजाश्च दक्षिणम् ।\nगोप्तारावर्जुनस्यैतावर्जुनोऽपि शिखण्डिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana again said to his brother: \"Yudhamanyu is the left wheel and Uttamauja the right; these two guard Arjuna, and Arjuna guards Shikhandin."}},{"n":22,"text":"स रक्ष्यमाणः पार्थेन तथास्माभिर्विवर्जितः ।\nयथा भीष्मं न नो हन्याद्दुःशासन तथा कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandin, protected by Partha and kept away from us, must not be allowed to kill Bhishma, Duhshasana; see to that.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"भ्रातुस्तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा पुत्रो दुःशासनस्तव ।\nभीष्मं प्रमुखतः कृत्वा प्रययौ सेनया सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his brother's words, your son Duhshasana put Bhishma in the front and marched forth with the army."}},{"n":24,"text":"भीष्मं तु रथवंशेन दृष्ट्वा तमभिसंवृतम् ।\nअर्जुनो रथिनां श्रेष्ठो धृष्टद्युम्नमुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Bhishma surrounded by a line of chariots, Arjuna, best of charioteers, said to Dhrishtadyumna:"}},{"n":25,"text":"शिखण्डिनं नरव्याघ्र भीष्मस्य प्रमुखेऽनघ ।\nस्थापयस्वाद्य पाञ्चाल्य तस्य गोप्ताहमप्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Faultless tiger among men, son of Panchala, place Shikhandin today in front of Bhishma, and I too will guard him.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"ततः शांतनवो भीष्मो निर्ययौ सेनया सह ।\nव्यूहं चाव्यूहत महत्सर्वतोभद्रमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhishma son of Shantanu came out with his army and drew up a great array in the battle, the one called sarvatobhadra."}},{"n":27,"text":"कृपश्च कृतवर्मा च शैब्यश्चैव महारथः ।\nशकुनिः सैन्धवश्चैव काम्बोजश्च सुदक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kripa, Kritavarman, the great chariot-warrior Shaibya, Shakuni, the king of Sindhu, and Sudakshina of the Kambojas,"}},{"n":28,"text":"भीष्मेण सहिताः सर्वे पुत्रैश्च तव भारत ।\nअग्रतः सर्वसैन्यानां व्यूहस्य प्रमुखे स्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"all together with Bhishma and your sons, Bharata, stood at the head of all the armies, in the front of the formation."}},{"n":29,"text":"द्रोणो भूरिश्रवाः शल्यो भगदत्तश्च मारिष ।\nदक्षिणं पक्षमाश्रित्य स्थिता व्यूहस्य दंशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, Bhurishravas, Shalya, and Bhagadatta, my lord, stood armoured on the right wing of the formation."}},{"n":30,"text":"अश्वत्थामा सोमदत्त आवन्त्यौ च महारथौ ।\nमहत्या सेनया युक्ता वामं पक्षमपालयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashvatthama, Somadatta, and the two great chariot-warriors of Avanti, with a great army, guarded the left wing."}},{"n":31,"text":"दुर्योधनो महाराज त्रिगर्तैः सर्वतो वृतः ।\nव्यूहमध्ये स्थितो राजन्पाण्डवान्प्रति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, great king, surrounded by the Trigartas on every side, stood in the middle of the formation, facing the Pandavas."}},{"n":32,"text":"अलम्बुसो रथश्रेष्ठः श्रुतायुश्च महारथः ।\nपृष्ठतः सर्वसैन्यानां स्थितौ व्यूहस्य दंशितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alambusa, best of charioteers, and the great warrior Shrutayu stood armoured at the rear of all the armies in the formation."}},{"n":33,"text":"एवमेते तदा व्यूहं कृत्वा भारत तावकाः ।\nसंनद्धाः समदृश्यन्त प्रतपन्त इवाग्नयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having drawn up their array in this way, Bharata, your men appeared fully armed, blazing like fires."}},{"n":34,"text":"तथा युधिष्ठिरो राजा भीमसेनश्च पाण्डवः ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च माद्रीपुत्रावुभावपि ।\nअग्रतः सर्वसैन्यानां स्थिता व्यूहस्य दंशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way King Yudhishthira, Bhimasena the Pandava, and Nakula and Sahadeva, the two sons of Madri, stood armoured at the front of all the armies."}},{"n":35,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नो विराटश्च सात्यकिश्च महारथः ।\nस्थिताः सैन्येन महता परानीकविनाशनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna, Virata, and the great chariot-warrior Satyaki, destroyers of enemy hosts, stood with a great army."}},{"n":36,"text":"शिखण्डी विजयश्चैव राक्षसश्च घटोत्कचः ।\nचेकितानो महाबाहुः कुन्तिभोजश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nस्थिता रणे महाराज महत्या सेनया वृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandin, Vijaya (Arjuna), the rakshasa Ghatotkacha, mighty-armed Chekitana, and valiant Kuntibhoja stood in the battle, great king, surrounded by a great army."}},{"n":37,"text":"अभिमन्युर्महेष्वासो द्रुपदश्च महारथः ।\nकेकया भ्रातरः पञ्च स्थिता युद्धाय दंशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great archer Abhimanyu, the great chariot-warrior Drupada, and the five Kekaya brothers stood armoured for battle."}},{"n":38,"text":"एवं तेऽपि महाव्यूहं प्रतिव्यूह्य सुदुर्जयम् ।\nपाण्डवाः समरे शूराः स्थिता युद्धाय मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus the brave Pandavas too, having drawn up a counter-array, huge and very hard to defeat, stood ready in the battle, my lord."}},{"n":39,"text":"तावकास्तु रणे यत्ताः सहसेना नराधिपाः ।\nअभ्युद्ययू रणे पार्थान्भीष्मं कृत्वाग्रतो नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your kings, intent on the fight, advanced with their armies against the Parthas, putting Bhishma in front, O king."}},{"n":40,"text":"तथैव पाण्डवा राजन्भीमसेनपुरोगमाः ।\nभीष्मं युद्धपरिप्रेप्सुं संग्रामे विजिगीषवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way the Pandavas, led by Bhimasena, advanced, eager for victory, against Bhishma, who longed for battle."}},{"n":41,"text":"क्ष्वेडाः किलिकिलाशब्दान्क्रकचान्गोविषाणिकाः ।\nभेरीमृदङ्गपणवान्नादयन्तश्च पुष्करान् ।\nपाण्डवा अभ्यधावन्त नदन्तो भैरवान्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With bellowing cries, shrieks, saws, cow-horn trumpets, kettledrums, mridangas, tabors, and drums sounding, the Pandavas ran forward, roaring terrible roars."}},{"n":42,"text":"भेरीमृदङ्गशङ्खानां दुन्दुभीनां च निस्वनैः ।\nउत्क्रुष्टसिंहनादैश्च वल्गितैश्च पृथग्विधैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the din of kettledrums, mridangas, conches, and drums, with lion-roars and various shouts and leaps,"}},{"n":43,"text":"वयं प्रतिनदन्तस्तानभ्यगच्छाम सत्वराः ।\nसहसैवाभिसंक्रुद्धास्तदासीत्तुमुलं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"we in turn roared back and went swiftly against them; suddenly, in great anger on both sides, there arose a mighty tumult."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततोऽन्योन्यं प्रधावन्तः संप्रहारं प्रचक्रिरे ।\nततः शब्देन महता प्रचकम्पे वसुंधरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, rushing at one another, they began the clash, and with that great noise the earth shook."}},{"n":45,"text":"पक्षिणश्च महाघोरं व्याहरन्तो विबभ्रमुः ।\nसप्रभश्चोदितः सूर्यो निष्प्रभः समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Birds wheeled about screaming fearfully, and the sun, rising bright, became dim."}},{"n":46,"text":"ववुश्च तुमुला वाताः शंसन्तः सुमहद्भयम् ।\nघोराश्च घोरनिर्ह्रादाः शिवास्तत्र ववाशिरे ।\nवेदयन्त्यो महाराज महद्वैशसमागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fierce winds blew, foretelling great terror, and dreadful jackals howled with terrible cries, announcing that great slaughter had come, O great king."}},{"n":47,"text":"दिशः प्रज्वलिता राजन्पांसुवर्षं पपात च ।\nरुधिरेण समुन्मिश्रमस्थिवर्षं तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The quarters seemed to blaze, O king, and a rain of dust fell, and likewise a rain of bones mixed with blood."}},{"n":48,"text":"रुदतां वाहनानां च नेत्रेभ्यः प्रापतज्जलम् ।\nसुस्रुवुश्च शकृन्मूत्रं प्रध्यायन्तो विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tears fell from the eyes of weeping horses and elephants, and the animals, brooding as it were, dropped dung and urine, lord of the people."}},{"n":49,"text":"अन्तर्हिता महानादाः श्रूयन्ते भरतर्षभ ।\nरक्षसां पुरुषादानां नदतां भैरवान्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great hidden cries were heard, bull of the Bharatas, of man-eating rakshasas howling terrible howls."}},{"n":50,"text":"संपतन्तः स्म दृश्यन्ते गोमायुबकवायसाः ।\nश्वानश्च विविधैर्नादैर्भषन्तस्तत्र तस्थिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jackals, herons, and crows were seen swooping down, and dogs stood there barking with many kinds of cries."}},{"n":51,"text":"ज्वलिताश्च महोल्का वै समाहत्य दिवाकरम् ।\nनिपेतुः सहसा भूमौ वेदयाना महद्भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great blazing meteors struck the sun and then suddenly fell to the ground, announcing great terror."}},{"n":52,"text":"महान्त्यनीकानि महासमुच्छ्रये\nसमागमे पाण्डवधार्तराष्ट्रयोः ।\nप्रकाशिरे शङ्खमृदङ्गनिस्वनैः\nप्रकम्पितानीव वनानि वायुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that great clash of the Pandavas and the Dhartarashtras, the vast armies, with the din of conches and mridangas, appeared like forests shaken by the wind."}},{"n":53,"text":"नरेन्द्रनागाश्वसमाकुलाना-\nमभ्यायतीनामशिवे मुहूर्ते ।\nबभूव घोषस्तुमुलश्चमूनां\nवातोद्धुतानामिव सागराणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that ill-omened hour, as those armies pressed on, crowded with kings, elephants, and horses, a tumultuous roar arose, like that of oceans lashed by a gale."}}]}]}